# Port missions, menus, roster, and progression after runtime completion

Port structured game content only after the runtime systems it invokes already
exist. This phase should leave the game functionally complete except for final
character/vehicle assets, their animation presentation, and later equivalence
polish.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Port all missions, objectives, conditions, triggers, races, collectibles,
  rewards, checkpoints, dialogue routing, and progression gates.
- [ ] Reproduce HUD, menus, navigation, character and vehicle roster data, and
  selection/unlock flows on the completed runtime.
- [ ] Bind normalized mission/UI/tuning/localization evidence to stable runtime
  APIs instead of using asset conversion as behavioral authority.
- [ ] Reach a start-to-finish functionally playable base before final asset
  completion becomes a blocker.

## Dependencies

Depends on completed runtime and rendering behavior.
